# Netscape HTTP Cookie File
# https://curl.se/docs/http-cookies.html
# This file was generated by libcurl! Edit at your own risk.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ClipFactory looks for a file named "cookies.txt" in the project root and
# passes it to yt-dlp (--cookies). It is OPTIONAL: only needed when YouTube
# demands sign-in for a video (age-gated, members-only, "confirm you're not a
# bot", or region-locked content).
#
# How to create your own cookies.txt
# ----------------------------------
# 1. Install a browser extension that exports Netscape-format cookies, e.g.
#    "Get cookies.txt LOCALLY" (Chrome/Firefox).
# 2. Sign in to YouTube with a THROWAWAY account. Do not use your main account.
# 3. Export the cookies for youtube.com and save the result as:
#       cookies.txt
#    in the project root (next to this example file).
# 4. Never commit it. "cookies.txt" is already listed in .gitignore.
#
# Alternatively use yt-dlp's built-in exporter:
#       yt-dlp --cookies-from-browser chrome --cookies cookies.txt
#
# Format reference (one tab-separated row per cookie):
#   domain  flag  path  secure  expiry  name  value
#
# Example row (placeholder values — NOT real credentials):
# .youtube.com	TRUE	/	TRUE	1893456000	EXAMPLE_COOKIE	placeholder-value
#
# Replace the example row with the rows your exporter produces, or simply
# delete it after exporting.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
